Subject: [PATCH] Admit one-shot candidate replies without a topology-state gate

OneWifi can return valid NaSta metrics within milliseconds while the agent
radio is reporting AP capabilities. The result command was admitted to the
radio queue but could not execute in that state, so it expired ten seconds
later, after the controller's HTTP measurement deadline. The timeout could
also cancel a newer sibling result of the same command type.

The result sender already sends synchronously, restores the original radio
state and marks its command finished. Admit that validated continuation in
any topology state, as for one-shot client presence notifications. Retain
radio exclusion, command locking, parser validation and the query MID.
Do not change native reporting periods, timeout budgets or policy margins.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
@@ -374,11 +374,7 @@
             return true;
         }
     } else if (pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_unassoc_sta_result) {
-        if ((em->get_state() == em_state_agent_topo_synchronized) ||
-            (em->get_state() == em_state_agent_configured) ||
-            (em->get_state() == em_state_agent_unassoc_sta_metrics_report_pending)) {
-            return true;
-        }
+        return true;
     }
 
     return false;
